mastery.solution_text:
Let the boat's still-water velocity be $a\underset{\sim}{i}+b\underset{\sim}{j}$ km/h.
The current is $-6\underset{\sim}{j}$, and the velocity relative to the bank must be due east, so its $\underset{\sim}{j}$ component is zero.
$b-6=0$
$b=6$
$a^{2}+6^{2}=10^{2}$
$a^{2}=64$
$a=8$
The boat steers $8$ east and $6$ north.
$\tan\theta=\frac{8}{6}$
$\theta=53.13^{\circ}$ east of north
Bearing
$=053^{\circ}$ to the nearest degree
Speed relative to the bank
$=8$ km/h
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (H) at (4.4,3.3);
\coordinate (G) at (4.4,0);
\draw[dashed,->] (O) -- (0,3.8) node[above] {$N$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (H) node[midway,above left] {$10$};
\draw[->,thick] (H) -- (G) node[midway,right] {$6$};
\draw[->,thick,dashed] (O) -- (G) node[midway,below] {$8$};
\draw ($(O)+(90:1.0)$) arc (90:{90-53.13}:1.0);
\node at ($(O)+({90-26.6}:1.55)$) {$53^{\circ}$};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
